-<div class="champ-banner"><p>🏈 <em>2026 CFP National Champions · 16-0 · Indiana Hoosiers</em> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Nothing But Time and Opinions &nbsp;·&nbsp; <em>I'll Ask For It</em></p></div><section class="list-hero"><div class="list-hero-inner"><p class="list-hero-label">Indianapolis · Top 10 List</p><h1 class="list-hero-title">Top 10 Things To Do in Indianapolis</h1><p class="list-hero-subtitle">These are the ten things you do before you can claim you really know the city.</p></div></section><section class="list-body"><div class="list-body-inner"><a href="index.html" class="back-link">← Back to Home</a><p class="list-intro">Indianapolis doesn't always get the credit it deserves. People fly through for a race or a convention and leave thinking they've seen it. They haven't. Here are the ten things that actually show you what the city is.</p><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">10</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Indianapolis Motor Speedway on Race Day</div><div class="list-item-desc">There is no experience in American sports quite like 300,000 people watching 33 cars take the green flag. The sound alone will change you. Do it at least once. Do it on the Sunday of Memorial Day weekend.</div><span class="list-item-note">Bucket List</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">09</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">The Indianapolis Museum of Art at Newfields</div><div class="list-item-desc">One of the top art museums in the country, attached to a 152-acre garden. The Lilly House. The 100 Acres outdoor sculpture park. The holiday lights. An embarrassment of riches in the middle of the city.</div><span class="list-item-note">Underrated Gem</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">08</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Walk the Cultural Trail</div><div class="list-item-desc">Eight miles of protected bike and pedestrian path connecting every major neighborhood. Fountain Square to Mass Ave to the Canal. The best way to understand how Indianapolis is stitched together.</div><span class="list-item-note">Best Two Hours</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">07</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Mass Ave on a Friday Night</div><div class="list-item-desc">Massachusetts Avenue has become the city's creative corridor. Galleries, restaurants, live music, a movie palace. Walk it on a Friday and you'll wonder when Indianapolis got so good at this.</div><span class="list-item-note">Must Do</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">06</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">A Game at Gainbridge Fieldhouse</div><div class="list-item-desc">One of the best arenas in the NBA, in a city that actually loves its team. The sightlines are perfect. Bankers Life hasn't existed for years but whatever they call it now still delivers.</div><span class="list-item-note">Game Night</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">05</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">The Children's Museum of Indianapolis</div><div class="list-item-desc">The largest children's museum in the world. Even if you don't have kids, the Dinosphere alone is worth an afternoon. The permanent collections are genuinely world-class.</div><span class="list-item-note">World Class</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">04</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Fountain Square on a Weekend</div><div class="list-item-desc">The neighborhood that time forgot and then remembered in the best way. Roller skating. Duckpin bowling. Live music. Restaurants that punch above their weight. The city at its most itself.</div><span class="list-item-note">Local Favorite</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">03</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Canal Walk at Sunset</div><div class="list-item-desc">The downtown canal is two miles of water, walking paths, and views of the city skyline that make you feel like Indianapolis earned its skyline. Rent a paddleboat. Walk it with a coffee. Either works.</div><span class="list-item-note">City Classic</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">02</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Indiana State Fair</div><div class="list-item-desc">Two weeks every August where Indiana shows up in full. Midway rides. Livestock competitions. Fried everything. The butter cow. It is not ironic appreciation — it's just good and it's ours.</div><span class="list-item-note">Annual Ritual</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">01</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Catch a Colts Game at Lucas Oil Stadium</div><div class="list-item-desc">One of the best stadiums in the NFL. Retractable roof. Downtown location. And now, a fan base that knows what a national championship season looks like. This is a different city than it was.</div><span class="list-item-note">New Energy</span></div></div></div></section><footer><div class="footer-inner">
+<div class="champ-banner"><p>🏈 <em>2026 CFP National Champions · 16-0 · Indiana Hoosiers</em> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Nothing But Time and Opinions &nbsp;·&nbsp; <em>I'll Ask For It</em></p></div><section class="list-hero"><div class="list-hero-inner"><p class="list-hero-label">Indy · Top 10 List</p><h1 class="list-hero-title">Top 10 Things To Do in Indianapolis</h1><p class="list-hero-subtitle">These are the ten things you do before you can claim you really know the city.</p></div></section><section class="list-body"><div class="list-body-inner"><a href="index.html" class="back-link">← Back to Home</a><p class="list-intro">Indianapolis doesn't always get the credit it deserves. People fly through for a race or a convention and leave thinking they've seen it. They haven't. Here are the ten things that actually show you what the city is.</p><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">10</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Indianapolis Motor Speedway on Race Day</div><div class="list-item-desc">There is no experience in American sports quite like 300,000 people watching 33 cars take the green flag. The sound alone will change you. Do it at least once. Do it on the Sunday of Memorial Day weekend.</div><span class="list-item-note">Bucket List</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">09</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">The Indianapolis Museum of Art at Newfields</div><div class="list-item-desc">One of the top art museums in the country, attached to a 152-acre garden. The Lilly House. The 100 Acres outdoor sculpture park. The holiday lights. An embarrassment of riches in the middle of the city.</div><span class="list-item-note">Underrated Gem</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">08</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Walk the Cultural Trail</div><div class="list-item-desc">Eight miles of protected bike and pedestrian path connecting every major