 end — a view, a waterfall, a moment of quiet you couldn't find anywhere else. These are the ten that kept their promise.</p><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">10</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Rim Trail — Grand Canyon South Rim, AZ</div><div class="list-item-desc">You can walk the entire South Rim on a paved trail and look into something that still doesn't make complete sense even when you're standing at the edge. Accessible. Overwhelming. Required.</div><span class="list-item-note">Must Walk</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">09</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Starved Rock State Park — Utica, IL</div><div class="list-item-desc">Eighteen canyons carved by glacial meltwater, two hours from Chicago. The canyon walls are sandstone. The waterfalls freeze solid in winter. It looks like something that shouldn't exist in Illinois.</div><span class="list-item-note">Midwest Surprise</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">08</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Brown County State Park Trails — Nashville, IN</div><div class="list-item-desc">Indiana's answer to the Smokies. Fall color that makes people drive three hours for it. The trails through the hills and hollers are what everyone who moved here from somewhere else didn't expect to find.</div><span class="list-item-note">Indiana Best</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">07</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Precipice Trail — Acadia National Park, ME</div><div class="list-item-desc">Iron rungs bolted into granite, exposed ledges, and a climb that's closer to via ferrata than hiking. It closes part of the season for nesting peregrine falcons, which tells you everything about who else thinks this cliff is worth claiming.</div><span class="list-item-note">Not for Everyone</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">06</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Tecumseh Trail — Morgan-Monroe State Forest, IN</div><div class="list-item-desc">The longest marked hiking trail in Indiana. Rugged for the Midwest. Quiet. The kind of trail that makes you realize Indiana has more vertical relief than people give it credit for.</div><span class="list-item-note">Long Haul</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">05</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Cliff Trail — Turkey Run State Park, IN</div><div class="list-item-desc">Rocky hollows, suspension bridges, ladders bolted into sandstone canyon walls. This is not a nature walk — it's an adventure. The best trails in Indiana are all in Turkey Run, and this is the best of those.</div><span class="list-item-note">Indiana Adventure</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">04</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Half Dome — Yosemite National Park, CA</div><div class="list-item-desc">The cables on the final pitch are steep enough to make your hands shake. The summit is worth every nerve. The valley view from the top justifies every permit application you ever filed.</div><span class="list-item-note">Classic</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">03</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Kalalau Trail — Nā Pali Coast, Kauai, HI</div><div class="list-item-desc">Eleven miles one-way along sea cliffs that shouldn't be walkable and somehow are. Permits required, exposure real, and Hanakāpīʻai Falls waiting at the halfway point for anyone not going the full distance. Nothing else looks like this.</div><span class="list-item-note">Bucket List</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">02</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Angels Landing — Zion National Park, UT</div><div class="list-item-desc">The chain section. The exposure. The drop on either side that makes you question every decision that brought you here. And then the summit. One of the most dramatic views in the American West, earned.</div><span class="list-item-note">Earn the View</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">01</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Appalachian Trail — Springer Mtn to Katahdin</div><div class="list-item-desc">2,190 miles of forest, mountain, and whatever you're made of. Most people do a section. The through-hikers who finish it are a different category of human. Even a week on it will rearrange how you think about distance.</div><span class="list-item-note">Life Changer</span></div></div></div></section><footer><div class="footer-inner"><div class="footer-brand"><div class="wordmark">I'll Ask <em>For It</em></div><div class="tagline">Nothing But Time and Opinions</div></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>Topics</h4><ul><li><a href="category-opinions.html">One Man's Opinion</a></li><li><a href="category-indy.html">Indy</a></li><li><a href="category-food.html">Food &amp; Drink</a></li><li><a href="category-music.html">Music</a></li><li><a href="category-sports.html">Sports</a></li><li><a href="category-travel.html">Worth the Trip</a></li><li><a href="category-nostalgia.html">Nostalgia</a></li><li><a href="hold-my-beer.html">Hold My Beer</a></li></ul></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>Top 10 Lists</h4><ul><li><a href="top10-restaurants.html">Restaurants</a></li><li><a href="top10-athletes.html">Athletes</a></li><li><a href="top10-things-to-do.html">Things To Do</a></li><li><a href="top10-trails.html">Trails</a></li><li><a href="top10-indy-sports.html">Indy Sports Moments</a></li><li><a href="top10-albums.html">Albums</a></li></ul></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>The Site</h4><ul><li><a href="about.html">About</a></li><li><a href="archive.html">Full Archive</a></li><li><a href="about.html#contact">Contact</a></li></ul></div></div><div class="foo